+# Ginux kernel/userspace contract coverage
+
+Generated from contract catalog version `2`. Do not edit this file by hand.
+
+The catalog is the reviewable inventory used to normalize instance contracts. An entry marked `partial` is deliberately bounded and does not claim complete Linux behavior. Operations absent from an effective contract are denied.
+
+## Summary
+
+| Status | Operations |
+|---|---:|
+| complete | 27 |
+| partial | 156 |
+| denied | 1 |
+| planned | 1 |
+| out-of-scope | 1 |
+| **Total** | **186** |
+
+## Versioned contract inputs
+
+- Primary input: one hierarchical `[contract]` recipe in the instance TOML
+- Surfaces: `syscalls`, `filesystem`, `network`, `devices`, `privileges`, `process`, and synthetic `kernel` views
+- Selectors: component-aware canonical operation selectors and bounded syscall-name globs compiled against this catalog
+- Precedence: default deny, broad grants, surface-specific grants, then explicit denies
+- Replaced inputs: `[userspace.*]` tables and execution-level dispatch fields fail closed
+- Runtime representation: an explicit operation table tied to catalog version `2` and a deterministic digest
+
+## Operation catalog
+
+| Operation | Kind | Linux ABI | Status | Default action | Direct-safe | Constraint | Evidence | Limitation |
+|---|---|---:|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| `syscall.read` | syscall | 0 | partial | mediate | no | bounded descriptor and length | `test-systemd` | x86-64 Linux ABI only |
+| `syscall.write` | syscall | 1 | partial | mediate | no | bounded descriptor and length | `test-systemd` | x86-64 Linux ABI only |
+| `syscall.open` | syscall | 2 | partial | mediate | no | instance path and validated flags | `test-native-vfs` | x86-64 Linux ABI only |
+| `syscall.close` | syscall | 3 | complete | mediate | no | instance descriptor | `test-systemd` | x86-64 Linux ABI only |
