+# Instance terminology migration
+
+## Source
+
+Human direction after accepting Gate 10: replace the active product term
+`domain` with `instance` before redesigning contract configuration and UX.
+
+## Goal
+
+Present one consistent `instance` concept across the active Ginux CLI,
+configuration, implementation, persistent state, audit output, tests, and
+documentation, with no supported legacy `domain` interface.
+
+## Approved scope
+
+- Replace `ginux domain ...` with `ginux instance ...` across every active CLI
+  and helper workflow.
+- Replace the `[domain]` TOML table and active schema/API terminology with
+  `[instance]` and instance-named types, fields, crates, modules, fixtures, and
+  examples where the term identifies the Ginux isolation unit.
+- Rename active persistent paths from `/var/lib/ginux/domains` to
+  `/var/lib/ginux/instances`, including lifecycle status, roots, caches, helper
+  arguments, and cleanup behavior.
+- Rename active audit fields, markers, logs, scripts, targets, configuration
+  filenames, and user-facing documentation to `instance` terminology.
+- Preserve technical uses of “domain” that do not name a Ginux instance, such
+  as DNS domain names, Unix domain sockets, protection domains, or external
+  source terminology.
+- Add deterministic stale-term checks over active product surfaces.
+- Preserve the accepted behavior and security invariants of Gates 1 through 10.
+
+## Non-goals
+
+- Backward-compatible `domain` CLI aliases, `[domain]` parsing, or migration of
+  existing `/var/lib/ginux/domains` state; this is an intentional clean break.
+- Editing locked records under `hdae/gates-done/` or rewriting Git history.
+- Changing contract semantics, instance behavior, or the underlying isolation
+  architecture.
+- Implementing the Gate 10.5 configuration and UX redesign.
+
+## Completed work
+
+- [x] Established the dedicated branch and carried the accepted Gate 10 closure
+  record onto merged `main` lineage.
+- [x] Renamed the CLI, TOML schema, Rust APIs and crate, persistence paths,
+  audit records, scripts, fixtures, examples, and active documentation.
+- [x] Added deterministic stale-term enforcement plus negative CLI and schema
+  checks for the unsupported legacy interface.
+- [x] Replaced internal OCI acquisition diagnostics in normal instance creation
+  with concise image, cache, bounded layer-progress, verification, and
+  preparation stages while retaining diagnostic output for low-level tooling.
+- [x] Propagated host terminal geometry into attached instance consoles on
+  initial attach and `SIGWINCH`, with full-screen and reattach regression
+  coverage.
+- [x] Removed shared-text software breakpoints from native child-ID
+  translation so multithreaded package workloads cannot mistake an internal
+  tracing mechanism for a workload trap and terminate the instance.
+- [x] Made bounded socket-tracking exhaustion local to the requesting socket
+  operation with `EMFILE`, and release tracked descriptors through
+  `close_range`, rather than failing the complete instance.
+- [x] Passed local, aggregate, targeted Rocky QEMU, and human-visible lifecycle
+  verification.
+
+## Remaining work
+
+- [x] Inventory and classify active `domain` terminology.
+- [x] Rename CLI, configuration schema, Rust APIs/crates, and persistent paths.
+- [x] Rename audit, scripts, tests, fixtures, examples, and active docs.
+- [x] Add stale-term and clean-break rejection tests.
+- [x] Run complete local and Rocky QEMU regression evidence.
+- [x] Deliver the branch and pull request for human review.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+- `ginux instance create/list/start/status/attach/stop` provides the accepted
+  lifecycle; `ginux domain` is rejected as an unknown command.
+- Active instance TOML uses `[instance]`; `[domain]` is rejected before launch.
+- Runtime state is stored beneath `/var/lib/ginux/instances`; active code and
+  tests do not create `/var/lib/ginux/instances`.
+- User-facing output and structured audit identify an `instance`, not a Ginux
+  `domain`.
+- Interactive instance creation presents a fixed-width live progress display
+  for image layers, suppresses redundant digests and internal paths, and gives
+  concise cache-hit and cache-miss summaries; noninteractive output remains
+  stable and line-oriented.
+- Active Rust package, module, type, field, function, script, fixture,
+  configuration, and documentation names consistently use `instance` when
+  referring to the isolation unit.
+- A bounded stale-term check rejects reintroduction on defined active surfaces
+  while excluding locked history and legitimate external technical meanings.
+- Gate 10 contract behavior, Rocky systemd boot, network controls, hooks,
+  lifecycle, and aggregate regressions remain passing.
+- `make demo-gate-10.25` exercises the human-visible instance lifecycle and
+  cleanly returns to the Rocky host.
+- Attached consoles inherit the caller's rows and columns, track subsequent
+  terminal resizes, and preserve correct geometry after full-screen programs
+  such as `vi` and after detach/reattach.
+- Multithreaded package-manager workloads do not encounter an internal Ginux
+  trace breakpoint, and bounded descriptor bookkeeping fails only the affected
+  operation rather than terminating the instance.
+
+## Verification plan
+
+- Terminology inventory and stale-term target -> no unapproved product use of
+  `domain` remains outside explicit exclusions.
+- Schema and CLI negative fixtures -> `[domain]` and `ginux domain` fail while
+  `[instance]` and `ginux instance` pass.
+- Persistent-state fixture -> lifecycle state exists only under
+  `/var/lib/ginux/instances`.
+- `make check` -> formatting and strict lint pass.
+- `make test-contract`, `make test-systemd`, Gate 9.75 network and hook tests,
+  and `make test` -> accepted behavior remains passing.
+- `make demo-gate-10.25` -> instance create/list/start/status/attach/stop,
+  terminology, rejection, and cleanup are observable and pass.
+
+## Evidence
+
+- Repository inventory on 2026-11-06 found 1,043 matching lines across 95
+  tracked files outside locked history before classification and migration.
+- `make check`, `make test-contract`, and `make test-unit` passed with the
+  renamed `ginux-instance` crate and active stale-term enforcement.
+- Rocky QEMU `make test-config`, `make test-instance`, `make test-systemd`,
+  `make test-gate975-network`, and `make test-gate975-hooks` passed.
+- A clean final `make test` aggregate passed after its first run found and the
+  implementation corrected a 13-to-15-byte fixture invariant introduced when
+  `domain-packet` became `instance-packet`.
+- `make demo-gate-10.25` passed create, list, status, start, attach, detach,
+  reattach, stop, persistent cache/state, legacy-schema rejection, and clean
+  return to the Rocky host. The live proof booted Rocky systemd to login and
+  stored runtime state exclusively under `/var/lib/ginux/instances`.
+- `make test-oci-image` passed all seven integrity, assembly, repeatability,
+  identity, corruption, offline, and layer-semantics checks after output modes
+  were separated.
+- `ROCKY_SSH_PORT=22410 make test-systemd-interactive` passed the complete
+  Rocky workflow alongside the human's active test VM. It exercised a fresh
+  cache miss with two fixed-width live layer bars, a cache hit without network
+  access, persistent reuse after host restart, and the complete instance
+  lifecycle.
+- A subsequent `ROCKY_SSH_PORT=22410 make test-systemd-interactive` run passed
+  terminal geometry propagation at `37x101`, opened and exited `vi` without
+  changing that geometry, then detached and reattached at `43x109`. Static
+  `make check` also passed.
+- An isolated Rocky QEMU run with `GINUX_INTERACTIVE_DNF_INSTALL=on` completed
+  the exact `dnf -y install vim` transaction without an unexpected trace stop
+  or instance exit, then passed job-control, proc, detach/reattach, controlled
+  shutdown, restart, persistent-cache, and lifecycle checks. The complete
+  `test-systemd-interactive` regression exited successfully, followed by a
+  clean `make check`.
+
+## Decisions and limitations
+
+- The migration is deliberately breaking because the project is still a
+  research prototype and maintaining two vocabularies would make the upcoming
+  UX redesign harder to understand and test.
+- Locked historical gate records retain the terminology under which their work
+  was reviewed and accepted.
+
+## Delivery strategy
+
+- Working branch: `hdae/domain-to-instance`
+- Intended base: `main`
+- Pull request: https://github.com/gmkurtzer/ginux/pull/235; never merge or
+  close without explicit authorization
+- Planned commits: establish gate and inventory; rename schema and Rust model;
+  rename CLI, persistence, and audit; migrate tests/docs and add stale-term
+  enforcement; record final evidence and PR
+- Actual commits: `464563e0` carries the accepted Gate 10 closure; `94f942ce`
+  performs the product-wide rename; `164dddf1` enforces the clean break;
+  `65a2646c` corrects rejection evidence; `d1f625ea` fixes the packet-length
+  invariant found by the aggregate regression; `44726568` polishes normal
+  instance image-acquisition output and its live progress display; `62569c66`
+  propagates terminal geometry and adds the full-screen regression; `da201188`
+  keeps multithreaded package workloads and bounded socket bookkeeping from
+  tearing down an instance
+
+## Review policy and outcome
+
+Human checkpoint. Present the complete stale-term inventory, interactive
+demonstration, fresh regression evidence, and pull request before acceptance.
