+# Intuitive self-contained contract configuration and UX
+
+## Source
+
+Human review of Gate 10 found that profiles, templates, and low-level operation
+identifiers provide a sound enforcement representation but are not an intuitive
+primary configuration interface.
+
+## Goal
+
+Let a human describe an instance's complete userspace contract in the same
+instance TOML using understandable access verbs, resource namespaces, and
+bounded globs, then inspect and explain exactly how that recipe compiles into
+the immutable Gate 10 operation table.
+
+## Approved scope
+
+- Add one self-contained `[userspace.contract]` configuration section with an
+  explicit version, catalog version, and default decision.
+- Add human-facing allow and deny groups for access verbs including read,
+  write, execute, connect, listen, process authority, and system authority.
+- Add documented canonical resource namespaces for filesystem paths, virtual
+  `/proc` and `/sys`, devices, networking, processes, signals, time, identity,
+  memory, and other Gate 10 catalog families.
+- Support bounded `*` single-component and `**` recursive selectors expanded
+  during validation, never matched dynamically at runtime.
+- Make deny rules deterministically override grants and fail closed on invalid,
+  ambiguous, or zero-match rules.
+- Compile the human recipe into the explicit immutable Gate 10 operation table,
+  provenance, and digest without weakening existing argument/resource checks.
+- Keep the complete recipe in one instance file. Complete examples may be
+  copied, but detached contract fragments and runtime preset dependencies are
+  not operator-facing concepts.
+- Provide `ginux instance` workflows to validate, inspect, explain, and diff
+  complete instance recipes with actionable diagnostics.
+- Treat every required instance configuration as a positional operand:
+  `create NAME FILE`, `validate FILE`, `inspect FILE`, and
+  `explain FILE OPERATION`. Optional typed overrides remain flags.
+- Preserve an explicitly marked advanced exact-operation escape hatch for
+  expert troubleshooting and workloads not expressible through the primary
+  vocabulary.
+- Add intuitive, self-contained filesystem constraints to the same recipe:
+  one absolute denied directory path applies to that path and every descendant
+  without matching neighboring path prefixes.
+- Add explicit recipe controls that disable set-ID semantics and device-node
+  creation while retaining ordinary FIFO creation where allowed.
+- Move distribution-specific bootstrap customization, including the temporary
+  root password, out of the host helper and into mediated `pre_boot` commands.
+- Treat operator-authored pre-boot commands as a bounded bootstrap phase: they
+  remain inside the instance root and syscall mediation, but final workload
+  path restrictions become active only after the hooks finish.
+- Reduce every native managed process at the host boundary. A root-launched
+  runtime uses host UID/GID 65534; a non-root runtime retains its caller UID/GID;
+  both set `PR_SET_NO_NEW_PRIVS` before executing managed code. Ginux virtual
+  credentials remain independent and authoritative inside the instance.
+
+## Non-goals
+
+- A graphical UI, browser service, remote policy service, or external policy
+  database.
+- Automatically granting observed behavior or silently weakening a recipe.
+- Runtime policy mutation.
+- Supporting legacy Gate 10 profile/template references as the primary saved
+  recipe; migration behavior will be defined before implementation.
+
+## Completed work
+
+- [x] Human approved the gate goal, self-contained recipe requirement, globbing
+  direction, and placement after the instance terminology migration.
+- [x] Gate 10.25 was accepted and merged; the terminology dependency is closed.
+- [x] Established dedicated branch `hdae/intuitive-contract-ux` from merged
+  `main` for the Gate 10.5 pull request.
+- [x] Defined the human resource vocabulary, access verbs, bounded selector
+  grammar, deny precedence, and exact-operation escape hatch.
+- [x] Defined migration ownership: complete example instance recipes are the
+  starting point, while legacy Gate 10 profiles remain internal
+  comparison-only compatibility input.
+- [x] Implemented recipe parsing, compilation, provenance, digesting,
+  diagnostics, CLI inspection workflows, runtime audit attribution, tests, and
+  the human demonstration.
+- [x] Migrated the strict-denial and Rocky systemd examples to self-contained
+  recipes and retained their accepted runtime behavior.
+- [x] Implement recursive path denial, disabled set-ID semantics, and explicit
+  device-node denial in the self-contained recipe.
+- [x] Move distro bootstrap customization into the Rocky example's mediated
+  pre-boot commands and remove its hardcoded root password from the helper.
+- [x] Enforce and verify the host UID/GID and `no_new_privs` backstop for every
+  managed native process.
+
+## Remaining work
+
+- [ ] Deliver the dedicated pull request for human review and acceptance.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+- One instance TOML completely describes the userspace contract without an
+  external template, profile file, or policy database.
+- Human rules compile reproducibly into the same explicit Gate 10 table and
+  digest, with provenance connecting every operation to its source rule.
+- `*` and `**` select only documented namespaces; malformed and zero-match
+  selectors fail before instance launch.
+- Deny precedence is deterministic and visible in check, show, explain, diff,
+  and runtime audit output.
+- Example instance recipes remain self-contained with no preset, profile file,
+  policy database, or detached contract object.
+- Advanced exact-operation rules cannot promote an unsupported operation or
+  bypass managed argument/resource validation.
+- Existing strict-denial and Rocky systemd behavior can be represented by
+  self-contained recipes and retain their Gate 10 runtime evidence.
+- `make demo-gate-10.5` validates, explains, compares, launches, and
+  audits representative recipes without hidden dependencies.
+- A single denied directory entry blocks writes to the directory and all
+  descendants, permits a neighboring prefix, and cannot be bypassed through
+  `..` or symlink traversal.
+- With set-ID disabled, managed code cannot add set-ID mode bits and executing
+  an image carrying them does not elevate virtual or host credentials.
+- Character and block device-node creation is denied explicitly; permitted
+  FIFO creation remains available.
+- Rocky bootstrap succeeds from recipe hooks, including the configured root
+  password, before final workload filesystem restrictions activate.
+- A root-launched native workload is visible on the host as UID/GID 65534 with
+  `NoNewPrivs: 1`; a non-root launch retains that caller's host UID/GID and also
+  has `NoNewPrivs: 1`. Instance-visible credentials continue to follow Ginux's
+  virtual credential model.
+
+## Verification plan
+
+- Parser/compiler unit matrix -> verb, namespace, glob, precedence, provenance,
+  digest, malformed-input, zero-match, and unsupported-promotion checks pass.
+- Migration fixtures -> accepted Gate 10 behaviors compile to equivalent final
+  operation decisions or expose an explicit reviewed incompatibility.
+- CLI tests -> instance validate/inspect/explain/diff output is deterministic,
+  concise, and actionable; the old top-level contract command is rejected.
+- Runtime negative fixture -> a high-level denial blocks the host effect and
+  records the winning human rule.
+- `make test-contract`, `make test-systemd`, and `make test` -> all mandatory
+  regressions pass.
+- `make demo-gate-10.5` -> complete human workflow and cleanup pass.
+- Filesystem-policy unit and native runtime fixtures -> recursive and
+  boundary-aware matching, traversal/symlink confinement, set-ID suppression,
+  device-node denial, FIFO control, and host-side UID/GID/no-new-privileges
+  assertions pass.
+- Rocky QEMU workflow -> mediated pre-boot setup, authenticated login,
+  read-only demo directory, writable neighboring directory, and systemd
+  regressions pass.
+
+## Evidence
+
+- Gate 10.25 pull request 235 was accepted and merged as `59e2f7aa`; its gate
+  record is closed and Gate 10.5 is no longer dependency-blocked.
+- `make check` and `make test-contract` pass with 12 contract tests and 19
+  instance tests, including bounded globs, aliases, malformed and zero-match
+  failure, deny precedence, unsupported-operation promotion rejection,
+  systemd authority equivalence, and recipe round-tripping.
+- `make test-config` passes in Rocky QEMU, including public `ginux instance`
+  validation, inspection, explanation, and diff of complete recipes without a
+  runtime preset reference.
+- `make test-contract-runtime` passes in Rocky QEMU: the human-facing
+  `deny[0]` rule blocks `syscall.socket`, the audit record reports that exact
+  source rule, and the attempted host mutation remains absent.
+- `make test-systemd` passes its cold, warm, repeated, offline, DNF-failure,
+  configured-failure, and shutdown matrix with the self-contained recipe.
+- The complete aggregate `make test` passes after the final migration and
+  documentation changes.
+- `make demo-gate-10.5` passes end to end with a 182-operation Rocky contract,
+  deterministic digest, explanation and diff output, runtime denial
+  provenance, and retained Rocky systemd behavior.
+- After human review removed the top-level contract namespace, fresh
+  `make check`, `make test-contract`, Rocky QEMU `make test-config`, aggregate
+  `make test`, and `make demo-gate-10.5` all pass. The public test exercises
+  `ginux instance validate|inspect|explain|diff` and proves `ginux contract`
+  is rejected.
+- Positional-configuration correction `b338e989` passes `make check`,
+  `make test-contract`, and isolated Rocky QEMU `make test-config`. The
+  interactive Rocky workflow rejects the former `create NAME --config FILE`
+  form, accepts `create NAME FILE`, acquires and reuses the OCI cache, and
+  reaches the Rocky systemd login. Its later proc identity check timed out in
+  that run; no create-path assertion failed.
+- The expanded Gate 10.5 implementation passes `cargo fmt --all -- --check`,
+  `cargo build -p ginux-init --target x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu --release`, all
+  21 `ginux-instance` tests, `make check`, `make test-contract`,
+  `make test-contract-runtime`, `make test-process`, `make test-systemd`, the
+  aggregate `make test`, and `make demo-gate-10.5`.
+- A clean isolated `make test-systemd-interactive` passes the recipe-owned
+  bootstrap, authenticated Rocky login, recursive and component-boundary path
+  denial, traversal and symlink confinement, hard-link and symlink creation
+  denial, set-ID denial, character-device denial, permitted FIFO creation,
+  root-origin host UID/GID 65534 with `NoNewPrivs: 1`, detach/reattach,
+  controlled shutdown, restart, and persistent cache reuse.
+- `make test-process` confirms that a non-root native launch retains every
+  real/effective/saved/filesystem UID and GID from its caller and has
+  `NoNewPrivs: 1`.
+- Pull-request CI exposed a Gate 1 fixture mismatch after host identity
+  reduction: its root-owned mode-0700 bind mount prevented the UID/GID 65534
+  tracee from reaching the payload before the expected exec stop. The fixture
+  now assigns its private mount to UID/GID 65534, preserving both the setup
+  failure assertions and the fail-open payload marker. Python syntax validation
+  passes locally. Pull-request `launch-integration` passes the corrected
+  Linux/root setup-failure matrix in 33 seconds; `static-and-unit` also passes.
+
+## Decisions and limitations
+
+- The human recipe is source of truth. The normalized operation table and
+  digest are derived immutable evidence, not a second hand-edited policy.
+- CLI configuration and explanation are the initial UI. A graphical UI is
+  deferred unless separately approved.
+- Access-verb groups classify catalog operations rather than weakening
+  operation-specific argument and resource checks. Unsupported catalog
+  authority cannot be promoted by either a glob or exact allow.
+- The systemd preset intentionally grants every supported operation in each
+  human access group and then denies raw packets and direct MMIO/DMA. This is
+  authority-equivalent to the accepted Gate 10 systemd contract; it is a
+  compatibility baseline, not a recommended least-authority recipe.
+- `setid = "deny"` disables elevation semantics rather than preventing an
+  otherwise permitted executable from running: setting set-ID bits is denied,
+  and existing set-ID bits confer no virtual or host privilege.
+- Pre-boot hooks are trusted instance configuration, not host hooks. Their
+  temporary bootstrap authority is limited to the mediated instance view and
+  ends before init starts.
+
+## Delivery strategy
+
+- Working branch: `hdae/intuitive-contract-ux` after Gate 10.25 acceptance
+- Intended base: `main` after Gate 10.25 merge
+- Pull request: intended; never merge or close without explicit authorization
+- Planned commits: vocabulary and schema; compiler and provenance; CLI UX;
+  migration/runtime fixtures; documentation, demo, and final evidence
+- Actual commits: `15a24849` closes the accepted dependency and starts the
+  gate; `cf68c612` adds recipes and compilation; `72df1f69` adds inspection
+  workflows; `40445fe2` migrates examples, documentation, and evidence;
+  `2d5e2dc7` moves all operator inspection under `ginux instance` and removes
+  fragment generation; `b338e989` makes required instance configurations
+  positional, including `instance create NAME FILE`; `39731fc2` adds recursive
+  filesystem constraints, recipe-owned bootstrap, set-ID and device-node
+  controls, and the least-privileged host execution backstop.
+
+## Review policy and outcome
+
+Human checkpoint because this gate defines the primary operator-facing security
+configuration and explanation model. Implementation and verification are
+complete; stop for review and acceptance before Gate 11.
