+# Contract maintenance lock
+
+## Source
+
+Human direction after Gate 12.25 to provide a safe host-side maintenance mode.
+
+## Goal
+
+Let an operator explicitly unlock a stopped instance for maintenance that its
+normal contract would deny, then relock it before ordinary use, with the state
+visible and persistent.
+
+## Approved scope
+
+- Add top-level `ginux lock NAME` and `ginux unlock NAME` commands.
+- Default every new and existing instance to locked contract enforcement.
+- Persist lock state as host deployment state, not portable recipe content.
+- Require the instance to be stopped before changing lock state.
+- In unlocked maintenance state, relax configurable contract restrictions for
+  supported operations while retaining Ginux virtualization, mediation,
+  unsupported-operation denial, host identity reduction, `NoNewPrivs`, and all
+  non-bypassable host-boundary invariants.
+- Display `locked` or `unlocked` in `ginux list` and `ginux status` and emit a
+  prominent warning when an unlocked instance starts.
+- Add deterministic CLI, persistence, policy, and Rocky maintenance tests plus
+  operator documentation.
+
+## Non-goals
+
+- Disabling Ginux, directly executing unsupported operations, granting host
+  credentials, exposing host `/proc` or `/sys`, or weakening mandatory host
+  containment.
+- Editing the portable instance recipe when lock state changes.
+- Allowing a running instance to change enforcement state.
+
+## Completed work
+
+- [x] Human approved the maintenance-state capability and autonomous delivery.
+- [x] Selected `lock` and `unlock` as the operator terminology.
+- [x] Implement persistent fail-closed deployment state and CLI commands.
+- [x] Materialize the bounded unlocked maintenance contract.
+- [x] Add presentation, warnings, documentation, and regressions.
+- [x] Run full focused, Rocky, systemd, and aggregate verification.
+
+## Remaining work
+
+- [x] Deliver the technically passed gate through its stacked pull request.
+- [x] Obtain human review and acceptance.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+- New instances and legacy deployment-state files without a lock record are
+  treated as locked.
+- `ginux unlock NAME` and `ginux lock NAME` work only while stopped, persist
+  atomically, and are idempotent.
+- `list` and `status` show the effective lock state, and starting unlocked emits
+  a warning that contract maintenance mode is active.
+- Locked execution uses the unchanged recipe contract; unlocked execution
+  admits supported maintenance operations such as package updates while still
+  denying unsupported and mandatory host-authority operations.
+- Relocking restores the exact recipe contract without modifying the recipe.
+- Malformed deployment state fails closed and no failed update changes state.
+- Existing lifecycle, contract, virtual filesystem, and systemd behavior
+  regressions remain green.
+
+## Verification plan
+
+- `make check` -> strict terminology, format, and lint pass.
+- CLI fixture -> default, idempotent, running-state rejection, persistence,
+  malformed-state rejection, list/status display, and warning assertions pass.
+- Contract fixture -> unlocked materialization broadens only supported policy
+  while mandatory denials and host-boundary invariants remain.
+- Rocky maintenance fixture -> a contract-denied mutation fails while locked,
+  succeeds while unlocked, and fails again after relocking.
+- `make test-config`, `make test-instance`, `make test-systemd`, and `make test`
+  -> complete regression evidence passes.
+- `make demo-gate-12.5` -> human-readable maintenance workflow passes.
+
+## Evidence
+
+- `make check` passed strict terminology, formatting, and lint checks.
+- `make test-gate125-lock` passed default and legacy fail-closed behavior,
+  atomic persistence, idempotence, running-state rejection, malformed-state
+  rejection, bounded maintenance materialization, exact relock restoration,
+  visibility, and warning assertions under Rocky QEMU.
+- `make test-systemd-interactive` passed the full clean-cache Rocky workflow.
+  A write beneath `/ginux-demo/read-only` failed while locked, succeeded during
+  an explicitly unlocked attached boot, and failed again after relocking. The
+  instance recipe was unchanged and host UID/GID reduction plus `NoNewPrivs`
+  remained active.
+- Fresh `make test-config`, `make test-instance`, `make test-systemd`, and
+  aggregate `make test` passed. The systemd matrix passed cold, warm, repeat,
+  offline, failed-DNF, configured-startup-failure, and controlled-shutdown
+  scenarios; prior interception, runtime, image, device, process, and virtual
+  kernel-view regressions also passed.
+- `make demo-gate-12.5` passed the operator-visible lock, unlock, maintenance,
+  and relock workflow.
+
+## Decisions and limitations
+
+- `lock`/`unlock` describes whether the recipe contract is enforced and is more
+  direct than “secure” or “enable.”
+- Unlock is an explicit maintenance state, not an enforcement bypass: Ginux
+  continues to own virtual kernel state and deny unsupported authority.
+- Lock state belongs to host deployment state because it is an operational
+  choice, not a portable workload requirement.
+
+## Delivery strategy
+
+- Working branch: `hdae/contract-maintenance-lock`
+- Intended base: `hdae/top-level-instance-cli`
+- Pull request: https://github.com/gmkurtzer/ginux/pull/254, stacked on Gate
+  12.25 pull request 253 and merged into `main` on 2026-11-09
+- Planned commits: gate record; deployment/CLI implementation; maintenance
+  policy and tests; evidence and pull-request checkpoint
+- Actual commits: `23784416` gate definition; `9891c38a` deployment state,
+  commands, bounded policy, presentation, documentation, and focused tests;
+  `e02f24cb` full Rocky maintenance lifecycle verification; `45515153`
+  verification evidence; and the merged pull-request checkpoint
+
+## Review policy and outcome
+
+Accepted and closed by the human during ledger reconciliation on 2026-11-11.
+Pull request 254 was merged into `main` on 2026-11-09 after the technical
+evidence passed.
