+- Boot-log audit -> classify the complete console and fail on any unallowlisted
+  Ginux-caused failure or warning signature.
+- `make check`, `make test-systemd`, the general interactive-host test,
+  `make test`, and `make demo-gate-9.5` -> all exit zero.
+
+## Evidence
+
+- Human reproduction before implementation: Bash emitted
+  `child setpgid (PID to PID): Operation not permitted`; `ps -ef` rejected the
+  synthetic `/proc`; detached runtime state required a trailing `systemd`
+  selector; and the systemd console contained compatibility diagnostics.
+- Repository inspection confirmed that `run-host` depended on the phony
+  `systemd-image-prepare` target and copied the assembled root into the VM;
+  syscall 109 accepted only `(0, 0)`; the native runtime mode selected systemd
+  from a trailing argument; and synthetic per-process proc materialization was
+  incomplete.
+- `make demo-gate-9.5` -> passed from an empty guest cache. First create
+  reported an OCI cache miss and ready state; a second create with image
+  networking disabled reported a cache hit. Login, simple/pipeline/background
+  jobs, `ps`, `/proc/self`, `Ctrl-]` detach, reattach, controlled shutdown,
+  detached lifecycle, and stale-state cleanup all passed.
+- `scripts/check-systemd-console.sh build/gate9-systemd-baseline.log` -> zero
+  unexpected compatibility diagnostics.
+- `make test-systemd` -> passed cold, warm, repeat, offline, deliberate DNF
+  failure, configured startup failure, and controlled shutdown checks.
+- `make check` and aggregate `make test` -> passed strict lint plus all unit,
+  interception, runtime, configuration, lifecycle, image, device, process, and
+  virtual-kernel-view regressions.
+- `make test-config` -> passed explicit missing-init and relative-init rejection
+  with `missing-field` and `invalid-value` diagnostics before launch.
+- Static validation of the persistent-state implementation passed shell syntax
+  checks, `git diff --check`, `make check`, and `make test-unit`.
+- `make test-systemd-interactive` -> passed from a clean isolated overlay. The
+  first create reported a cache miss, displayed live percentage progress for
+  both OCI layers, and passed an offline same-session hit. After host shutdown,
+  the second boot reused the same overlay, retained `rocky` in stopped state,
+  and created `restart-cache` offline with `OCI_CACHE: hit`.
+- Human reproduction after that run: `time ps -ef` required 1.871 seconds for
+  five virtual tasks and printed corrupt user/system durations. Inspection
+  found that every `/proc` or `/proc/<pid>/...` open called
+  `native_proc_refresh_all`, repeatedly sampling and rewriting every virtual
+  task and global file during one `ps` traversal.
+- The corrected clean QEMU run measured `ps -ef` at 309 ms and a single
+  `top -b -n 1` refresh at 913 ms. Bash reported valid `real`, `user`, and
+  `sys` durations of 0.207, 0.007, and 0.036 seconds. A preceding isolated run
+  measured `ps -ef` at 273 ms, confirming that the result is repeatable and
+  not a one-off warm-path observation.
+- `make test-systemd-interactive` -> passed the new one-second `ps` and `top`
+  budgets while retaining live virtual task, CPU, and RSS accounting. It also
+  passed the cold OCI acquisition, same-session offline hit, persistent-domain,
+  restart, and second-session offline-hit checks.
+- `make test-systemd` -> passed cold, warm, repeat, offline, deliberate DNF
+  failure, configured startup failure, and controlled shutdown checks after
+  the proc refresh change.
+- Aggregate `make test` -> passed strict checks plus all unit, interception,
+  runtime, configuration, domain, image, device, process, and virtual-kernel-
+  view regressions after the proc refresh change.
+- Human checkpoint on 2026-11-06 -> Gate 9.5 accepted together with Gate 9
+  after the interactive general-host workflow and final evidence review.
+
+## Decisions and limitations
+
+- Bash uses `setpgid(child_pid, child_pid)` because its parent establishes a
+  new process group for the forked job. Zero arguments are shorthand for the
+  calling process and its PID; they are not the only valid Linux form.
+- Procfs remains a Ginux-owned compatibility view. Passing the host proc mount
+  through would violate the project boundary and is not an acceptable fix.
+- `Ctrl-]` is the human-selected detach sequence.
+- Boot-log cleanup must repair semantics, not suppress arbitrary output.
+- Rocky systemd emits one accurate optional-feature diagnostic because Ginux
+  does not expose a BPF LSM. Ginux does not falsely advertise that kernel
+  feature; the exact line is narrowly allowlisted and every other matching
+  warning or failure fails the console audit.
+- Virtual `cgroup.procs` writes are mediated rather than retained as static
+  file contents, so exited virtual tasks do not remain visible during shutdown.
+  Full resource-controller semantics remain outside this corrective gate.
+- The writable Rocky QCOW2 overlay is reused by `make run-host`, so verified
+  OCI content, domain roots, configurations, and last status survive. Explicit
+  `make clean` remains the reset mechanism and removes that overlay.
+- The latency budget is a compatibility regression under x86-64 QEMU TCG on
+  Apple Silicon, not a native-performance claim. Synthetic proc data remains
+  Ginux-owned and is refreshed on demand for the requested global or task file.
+- Linux x86-64 presents `RUSAGE_CHILDREN` to the traced syscall as a
+  zero-extended 32-bit `-1`; Ginux accepts that ABI form while continuing to
+  reject unsupported `getrusage` selectors.
+
+## Delivery strategy
+
+- Working branch: `hdae/systemd-usability`
+- Intended base: `hdae/systemd-baseline` until Gate 9 is accepted and merged;
+  retarget to `main` afterward
+- Pull request: the implementation was integrated into `main` through signed
